  "worked_solution": "A similarity transformation is any transformation made up of rigid motions (rotations, reflections, and translations) and dilations. \n\nA similarity transformation will map any polygon to a similar polygon.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We are given a combination of a reflection and a translation. As a result, we obtain that \n\n$$\nABCD∼PQRS.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since our combined transformation consists of rigid motions only (namely, reflections), the distance between all points is preserved under the transformation. Therefore,  we obtain that \n\n$$\nABCD≅PQRS.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $ABCD≅PQRS,$ all corresponding sides must be congruent. In particular, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{BC}≅\\overset{―}{QR}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
